    "intro_html":  "Moussaka is the Greek answer to lasagna, except the layers are roasted eggplant instead of pasta and the top is a thick bechamel that puffs and browns in the oven. It bakes in one pan and cuts into clean squares, which is exactly what you want when you are portioning out a week. Each square lands at {{cal}} calories and \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
